WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.023
Zann let out a yell, and Zing let out a blast of flame before they both realized who had just burst into the cave.

2
00:00:07.024 --> 00:00:12.501
"Perda!" Zann exclaimed. "You shouldn't sneak up on people like that!"

3
00:00:12.502 --> 00:00:19.394
She smirked, quickly rubbing her fingers together and touching her arm to repair the spot where Zing had just singed her.

4
00:00:19.395 --> 00:00:23.976
"If you didn't want me in here, you should have used a Shield spell," she said.

5
00:00:23.977 --> 00:00:31.098
"What's the point?" Zann said. "You know all my passwords. You'd get past a Shield spell too."

6
00:00:31.099 --> 00:00:35.981
"True." Perda's smile faded quickly, and her eyes filled with worry.

7
00:00:35.982 --> 00:00:40.459
"But listen, I'm glad I found you. Did you know your house—"

8
00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:46.622
"Just blew up?" Zann finished grimly. "Yes. Zing and I barely got away."

9
00:00:46.623 --> 00:00:49.937
"What about Boz?" Perda asked anxiously.

10
00:00:49.938 --> 00:00:54.326
"I don't think he was there," Zann said. "Here's what happened . . ."

11
00:00:54.327 --> 00:00:57.488
He told her the same story he'd just told Darb.

12
00:00:57.489 --> 00:01:04.767
Perda listened quietly. "Wow," she said when Zann had finished. "And you didn't recognize the guy?"

13
00:01:04.768 --> 00:01:08.641
"I've never seen him before in my life," Zann replied.

14
00:01:08.642 --> 00:01:10.591
"Did you check the Directory?"

15
00:01:10.592 --> 00:01:13.257
Zann blinked. Why hadn't he thought of that?

16
00:01:13.258 --> 00:01:18.408
"Um, not yet," he said, shooting a sheepish glance toward Darb.

17
00:01:18.409 --> 00:01:21.761
"We, uh, were just about to do that."

18
00:01:21.762 --> 00:01:25.113
"Here, I'll pull it up." Perda snapped her fingers.

19
00:01:25.114 --> 00:01:33.119
A book-like image appeared in midair, floating at eye level. "Identification needed," Zann said. "Adult male."

20
00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:37.997
Instantly the book disappeared, replaced by a long list of names.

21
00:01:37.998 --> 00:01:44.067
The names were in tiny print, since they represented every adult male in Magica.

22
00:01:44.068 --> 00:01:50.482
A picture floated beside each name, though the images were far too minuscule to be seen clearly.

23
00:01:50.483 --> 00:01:55.603
For a second Zann was tempted to check the list and see if his father was listed, or Boz.

24
00:01:55.604 --> 00:02:00.119
But he resisted the temptation. He had checked his father's listing before.

25
00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:07.500
It was still there, but with a special notation at the top: "Missing, presumed deceased or permanently off-world."

26
00:02:07.501 --> 00:02:13.932
As for Boz, it was too soon for his Directory status to have changed, no matter what had happened.

27
00:02:13.933 --> 00:02:19.538
"Well?" Perda said, sounding impatient. "Is there anything else you can remember about this guy?

28
00:02:19.539 --> 00:02:22.186
You need to narrow the search down a little."

29
00:02:22.187 --> 00:02:27.239
"I know, I'm just thinking." Zann tried to remember what the stranger had looked like.

30
00:02:27.240 --> 00:02:34.504
"Uh, taller than average. Thinner than average. Between thirty and fifty years old."

31
00:02:34.505 --> 00:02:44.023
He watched as the list rearranged itself, the names getting bigger as their numbers became fewer. "Pale skin. Long, thinning dark hair."

32
00:02:44.024 --> 00:02:47.021
"What color were his eyes?" Perda prompted.

33
00:02:47.022 --> 00:02:53.194
"I'm trying to remember. I wasn't exactly gazing into his eyes at the time, you know," Zann said.

34
00:02:53.195 --> 00:02:57.342
"Here, I'll help." Perda held out both her hands.

35
00:02:57.343 --> 00:03:02.677
"Help with what?" Zann understood that she was offering to combine her magic with his.

36
00:03:02.678 --> 00:03:05.402
Anyone could do that to make a spell stronger.

37
00:03:05.403 --> 00:03:09.880
What he didn't understand was what spell she thought they should do.

38
00:03:09.881 --> 00:03:14.919
Perda sighed. "Don't you ever pay attention in Mental Magic class?

39
00:03:14.920 --> 00:03:19.074
We just covered Enhanced Short-term Memory spells last month!"

40
00:03:19.075 --> 00:03:23.976
"Oh, right." Zann lifted his own hands and rubbed his palms against hers.

41
00:03:23.977 --> 00:03:31.575
Sparks began to crackle between them. "Recall," he murmured, trying to focus on the memory of the man's face.

42
00:03:31.576 --> 00:03:34.161
Just like that the image popped into his head.

43
00:03:34.162 --> 00:03:37.976
It was as clear as if the stranger were standing right in front of him.

44
00:03:37.977 --> 00:03:41.744
Zann shuddered, quickly dropping his hands from Perda's.

45
00:03:41.745 --> 00:03:52.461
"Amber eyes," he said. "Small, mean-looking amber eyes, to be precise. Narrow face with sunken cheeks."

46
00:03:52.462 --> 00:03:55.977
He went on, adding as many details as he could.

47
00:03:55.978 --> 00:03:59.131
With each one the list of names grew shorter.

48
00:03:59.132 --> 00:04:02.722
Soon there were only a few names left on the floating screen.

49
00:04:02.723 --> 00:04:07.344
By now both names and images were large enough to see easily.

50
00:04:07.345 --> 00:04:11.881
"Do you recognize any of the pictures?" Darb asked, peering at the Directory.

51
00:04:11.882 --> 00:04:15.720
"I'm not sure . . ." Zann scanned the entries.

52
00:04:15.721 --> 00:04:20.911
"Wait! There he is—that's him!" Zann pointed at one of the images.

53
00:04:20.912 --> 00:04:25.779
Instantly all the other entries dropped away. "Full entry, please."

54
00:04:25.780 --> 00:04:28.875
More words appeared beneath the name and picture.

55
00:04:28.876 --> 00:04:37.957
"'Name: Morb,'" Perda read. "'Home: Dragon's Peak, Mount Mystery. Current Occupation: Unknown.'"

56
00:04:37.958 --> 00:04:44.247
"Dragon's Peak?" Zann said. "Isn't that the village that's always having trouble with trolls?"

57
00:04:44.248 --> 00:04:48.251
"Wait, this can't be the right person after all," Darb spoke up.

58
00:04:48.252 --> 00:04:52.479
"Look—he's a Void." He pointed to another part of the entry.

59
00:04:52.480 --> 00:04:56.601
"A Void?" Zann echoed. "But that doesn't make sense.

60
00:04:56.602 --> 00:05:00.149
This is definitely the guy that was at my house.

61
00:05:00.150 --> 00:05:05.841
Yet there's no way a Void could do what he did! The entry must be wrong."

62
00:05:05.842 --> 00:05:09.557
Perda moved her hand, causing the Directory to scroll down.

63
00:05:09.558 --> 00:05:14.513
"It can't be wrong," she said. "There are lots of mentions of him being a Void.

64
00:05:14.514 --> 00:05:20.092
See? It even says he used to work as an animal caretaker. That's a Void job."

65
00:05:20.093 --> 00:05:24.363
Zann glanced at the entry. "Wait, go back," he said.

66
00:05:24.364 --> 00:05:31.343
"Check it out. This Morb guy used to work at my parents' research laboratory at the university!"

67
00:05:31.344 --> 00:05:36.885
"Really? Then maybe Morb isn't connected to the royal warning at all," Perda suggested.

68
00:05:36.886 --> 00:05:39.879
"He might have been looking for your parents or something."

69
00:05:39.880 --> 00:05:42.544
"But he said he knew where Boz was.

70
00:05:42.545 --> 00:05:48.206
And why would he try to use the Flash Freeze on me? That doesn't make any sense."

71
00:05:48.207 --> 00:05:53.935
"Zann's right. This has to be connected to the disappearances of Reds somehow," Darb said.

72
00:05:53.936 --> 00:05:58.657
"I guess you're right." Perda gasped. "Gliss!"

73
00:05:58.658 --> 00:06:00.549
"Huh?" Zann said.

74
00:06:00.550 --> 00:06:04.730
"She's a Red, and so are both her parents," Perda said.

75
00:06:04.731 --> 00:06:14.276
"If Morb is after Reds, he'll probably try to get them too. We have to warn her!"

